<p>The same 600 km, two-day Coorg trip in the 12 seater Maharaja Tempo Traveller costs 600 × ₹22 = ₹13,200 plus ₹1,000 Bata, about ₹14,200, or roughly ₹1,183 per person. The Maharaja Urbania costs about ₹10,000 more for the whole trip, which is about ₹833 more per person. That is the price of the quieter ride, the business-class recliners, the Smart TV and the cold storage. For some groups, such as VIP guests, it is an easy decision. For others, it is not, and the Tempo Traveller is the sensible pick. We would rather you chose the vehicle that suits your budget and your guests.</p>

<h3>How the cost looks per hour of comfort</h3>
<p>A useful way to judge the premium is to divide it by time. A two-day Coorg trip involves about 12 to 14 hours in the vehicle. A premium of about ₹833 per person over 12 to 14 hours is roughly ₹60 to ₹70 per person per hour for a business-class cabin. If your group is going to spend those hours together, this is often an acceptable price. If the trip is a one-hour airport run, the premium buys much less.</p>

<h3>Tips for keeping the cost sensible</h3>
<ul>
<li>Fill all 12 seats where you can. The cost is for the vehicle, so each additional passenger lowers the cost per head.</li>
<li>Use the daily minimum. Since 300 km is billed anyway, plan a nearby stop on the same day.</li>
<li>Finish the day before 10:00 PM to avoid extra Bata.</li>
<li>Book early for weekends and festivals, so you get the vehicle you want and not a substitute.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Part 5. Luxury Itineraries from Bangalore for a Group of 12</h2>
<p>These sample itineraries show how the vehicle fits real trips. They are plans to adapt, not fixed packages. Distances and times are approximate.</p>

<h3>One day: Mysore in comfort</h3>
<p>Leave Bangalore at 6:30 AM. Reach Mysore by about 10:00 AM after a breakfast stop. Visit the Mysore Palace, then Chamundi Hills and lunch in the city. In the afternoon, visit the Brindavan Gardens or the local markets and leave by 5:00 PM, reaching Bangalore in the evening. The round trip is under 300 km, so the 300 km daily minimum applies and the total before extras is about ₹12,100. This is the easiest way to try the vehicle.</p>

<h3>Two days: Coorg weekend</h3>
<p>Day one, leave early and reach Coorg by lunchtime, with a stop at the Namdroling Monastery at Bylakuppe on the way. Check in, then visit Abbey Falls and Raja's Seat for sunset. Day two, visit Dubare or Talacauvery, shop for coffee and spices in Madikeri and begin the return mid-afternoon. About 600 km is billed, and the total before extras is about ₹24,200. See the <a href="/tour-packages/coorg-getaway">Coorg Getaway</a> and our <a href="/blog/bangalore-to-coorg-road-trip-itinerary-tempo-traveller">Coorg road trip itinerary</a>.</p>

<h3>Two days: Chikmagalur and the coffee hills</h3>
<p>Day one, drive to Chikmagalur and settle into a coffee estate stay. Day two, visit Mullayanagiri or Baba Budangiri early for the view, see Hebbe Falls and return. The total before extras is about ₹24,200 for the 600 km minimum. See the <a href="/tour-packages/chikmagalur-coffee-trails">Chikmagalur Coffee Trails</a>.</p>

<h3>Three days: Ooty and Coonoor</h3>
<p>Day one, drive to Ooty, crossing the forest check-posts in daylight. Day two, visit the Botanical Garden, the lake, Doddabetta and tea estates around Coonoor. Day three, return. The distance is about 550 km round trip plus local sightseeing, so the vehicle will likely exceed the 300 km a day minimum for a three-day trip only if the local driving is long. Check the billed distance in your quotation. See the <a href="/tour-packages/ooty-coonoor-hill-tour">Ooty and Coonoor Hill Tour</a>.</p>

<h3>Three days: Wayanad nature escape</h3>
<p>Day one, drive to Wayanad. Day two, visit Edakkal Caves, Banasura Sagar and Soochipara Falls. Day three, a slow morning and the return drive. Interstate permits and state taxes apply as the route enters Kerala. See the <a href="/tour-packages/wayanad-nature-escape">Wayanad Nature Escape</a>.</p>

<h3>Three days: Hampi heritage</h3>
<p>Day one, drive to Hampi. Day two, a full day at the Virupaksha temple, the Vittala temple and the Royal Enclosure, ideally at sunrise and late afternoon to avoid the heat. Day three, return. The round trip is about 690 km, and the three-day minimum is 900 km, so 900 km is billed, about ₹36,300 before extras. See the <a href="/tour-packages/hampi-heritage-trail">Hampi Heritage Trail</a>.</p>

<h2>Part 6. Airport Transfers with the Maharaja Urbania</h2>
<p>A premium vehicle for an airport transfer is a common use. Kempegowda International Airport is on the north side of Bangalore, and the journey to areas like Whitefield, Electronic City or Koramangala can take an hour or much longer in peak traffic. The Maharaja Urbania makes that transfer easier for a small delegation or a family returning from abroad.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Share the flight number.</strong> The driver tracks the flight and adjusts for delays.</li>
<li><strong>Agree the meeting point.</strong> Tell the group exactly where the driver waits.</li>
<li><strong>Plan for luggage.</strong> A full flight arrival may carry more than 12 bags. Tell us the count.</li>
<li><strong>Plan the destination.</strong> Give the full address and a contact number for the drop.</li>
</ul>
