<h2>Part 7D. More Trip Ideas for a Group of 12</h2>

<h3>Sakleshpur and the Western Ghats</h3>
<p>Sakleshpur sits in the Western Ghats between Bangalore and the coast and is known for green hills, coffee and spice estates and the Manjarabad Fort. It is a restful two-day trip for a small family group. The drive is under five hours in good traffic. The ghat sections through the hills are scenic and best crossed in daylight. See <a href="/rent/force-urbania/bangalore-city-to-sakleshpur">Urbania Bangalore to Sakleshpur</a> and the <a href="/tour-packages/sakleshpur-western-ghats-trail">Sakleshpur Western Ghats Trail</a>.</p>

<h3>Kabini wildlife weekend</h3>
<p>Kabini is built around the Kabini river and the Nagarhole forest. A group of 12 can take a resort stay and morning and evening safaris, which are scheduled by the forest authorities. Confirm the safari slot with the resort and plan to arrive in time for check-in. The Urbania's quiet cabin is a pleasant way to arrive after a long drive. See <a href="/rent/force-urbania/bangalore-city-to-kabini">Urbania Bangalore to Kabini</a>.</p>

<h3>Pondicherry and Auroville</h3>
<p>Pondicherry is known for its French quarter, the seafront promenade and cafes, and Auroville for its community and the Matrimandir. The route enters Tamil Nadu and Puducherry, so permits and state taxes apply. A three-day plan gives time for the drive and a relaxed stay. See <a href="/rent/force-urbania/bangalore-city-to-pondicherry">Urbania Bangalore to Pondicherry</a>.</p>

<h3>Nandi Hills sunrise</h3>
<p>Nandi Hills is the shortest escape from Bangalore, popular for sunrise views. A small group can leave before dawn, watch the sunrise and return for breakfast in the city. Because the round trip is far below the 300 km daily minimum, the vehicle is billed at 300 km for the day. See the <a href="/tour-packages/nandi-hills-sunrise-trip">Nandi Hills Sunrise Trip</a>. Entry timings and vehicle rules at the hill are set by the authorities, so confirm them before you go.</p>

<h3>Lepakshi</h3>
<p>Lepakshi in Andhra Pradesh is known for the Veerabhadra temple, with its hanging pillar and large Nandi bull. It is a good one-day trip for heritage-minded groups and is reached from northern Bangalore, such as <a href="/urbania-rent-yelahanka">Yelahanka</a> or <a href="/urbania-rent-hebbal">Hebbal</a>, in a little under three hours. As the route crosses the state border, permits and taxes apply.</p>

